WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.459 --> 00:00:06.440
Created by Jack Kirby and Stan Lee in 1963's
The X-Men #4, Wanda Maximoff, the Scarlet

00:00:06.440 --> 00:00:09.020
Witch, has some of the strangest stories in
comics.

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:13.719
From her mechanical ex-husband to the many,
many retcons of who her father is, here are

00:00:13.720 --> 00:00:16.280
things Marvel wants you to forget about the
Scarlet Witch.

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:18.500
What even is Chaos Magic?

00:00:18.820 --> 00:00:22.940
Scarlet Witch started out as a mutant who
had "hex powers," which basically meant that

00:00:22.940 --> 00:00:24.780
she could do anything that the writer wanted.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:29.300
Beyond wearing all red, Wanda Maximoff really
wasn't much of a Scarlet Witch at all.

00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:32.140
She wasn't even scarlet on her first cover
appearance.

00:00:32.349 --> 00:00:36.640
She wasn't truly witchy until writer Steve
Englehart had her study magic under Agatha

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:42.060
Harkness — an actual witch — in 1974's
The Avengers #128.

00:00:42.260 --> 00:00:46.280
Later stories would establish that she was
gifted at magic because Chthon, the Marvel

00:00:46.289 --> 00:00:50.750
universe equivalent to Cthulhu, molded her
at birth to be the perfect vessel for his

00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:51.460
physical form.

00:00:51.750 --> 00:00:56.520
Add in later retcons involving chaos magic
and reality warping, and her powers have remained

00:00:56.540 --> 00:00:59.249
as ambiguous today as they were when she first
appeared.

00:00:59.320 --> 00:01:03.159
"Her thing is neuroelectric interfacing telekinesis
and mental manipulation."

00:01:04.760 --> 00:01:06.040
"He's fast and she's weird."

00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:07.940
Who's your daddy?

00:01:08.340 --> 00:01:12.820
While Wanda and her brother Pietro are popularly
known as the children of Magneto, that hasn't

00:01:12.820 --> 00:01:13.920
always been the case.

00:01:14.070 --> 00:01:19.360
In 1974's Giant-Size Avengers #1, it's established
that they were the children of the Whizzer

00:01:19.360 --> 00:01:22.720
and Miss America, superheroes from Marvel's
Golden Age.

00:01:22.840 --> 00:01:26.840
Wanda learns that, years ago, the Whizzer
had brought his pregnant wife to Wundagore

00:01:26.840 --> 00:01:29.520
Mountain, where she died after delivering
twins.

00:01:29.689 --> 00:01:34.500
Notably, this delivery occurred under the
watchful eye of the High Evolutionary, a geneticist

00:01:34.500 --> 00:01:37.070
obsessed with, as his name suggests, evolution.

00:01:37.360 --> 00:01:40.620
Bova, a talking cow woman, delivered Wanda
and Pietro.

00:01:40.680 --> 00:01:42.060
Because comics are weird.

00:01:42.180 --> 00:01:46.620
This would be retconned in 1979's The Avengers
#185.

00:01:46.900 --> 00:01:51.969
In this version, a pregnant woman named Magda
appears at Wundagore Mountain to deliver twins,

00:01:51.969 --> 00:01:53.140
Pietro and Wanda.

00:01:53.380 --> 00:01:59.080
After she disappears, the High Evolutionary
gives them away to a traveling Romani family,

00:01:59.080 --> 00:02:03.040
the Maximoffs, who raises them until Wanda
and Pietro join Magneto shortly before X-Men

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:03.540
#4.

00:02:04.040 --> 00:02:06.260
"When brought to our home by a midwife.

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:08.980
Her name was Bova.

00:02:09.760 --> 00:02:14.320
A most wondrous creature, part-human, part-animal."

00:02:15.020 --> 00:02:16.560
Seriously, who's your daddy?

00:02:16.720 --> 00:02:21.920
Magneto was officially confirmed to be their
father in 1983's The Vision and Scarlet Witch

00:02:21.920 --> 00:02:26.860
#4, finally answering the lingering question
of who Wanda's biological father was.

00:02:26.860 --> 00:02:28.380
But that wasn't the end of it.

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:31.720
"We are not your natural parents."

00:02:32.260 --> 00:02:33.280
"What are you saying?"

00:02:33.500 --> 00:02:38.280
In 2014's AXIS, Wanda discovered that Magneto
wasn't actually her father.

00:02:38.280 --> 00:02:42.300
Later, she discovered later that she and Pietro
weren't actually ever mutants at all, but

00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:46.090
regular humans who had been experimented on
by the High Evolutionary at birth to create

00:02:46.090 --> 00:02:47.360
superpowered siblings.

00:02:47.580 --> 00:02:52.460
In this most recent retcon, Wanda's biological
family is currently settled to be the Maximoffs.

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:57.100
Coincidentally, that revelation happened right
around the time that Twentieth Century Fox

00:02:57.110 --> 00:03:01.810
had established that they owned the film rights
to both Magneto and "mutants" as a concept

00:03:01.810 --> 00:03:03.580
… but there's probably no connection.

00:03:04.260 --> 00:03:05.240
Demon babies

00:03:05.940 --> 00:03:08.940
For a while, Wanda was married to the "synthozoid"
Avenger, Vision.

00:03:08.940 --> 00:03:12.040
They even managed to have twins together through
Wanda's magic.

00:03:12.390 --> 00:03:16.480
Unfortunately, it turned out that while the
children technically existed, they only existed

00:03:16.480 --> 00:03:18.590
while Wanda was actively thinking of them

00:03:18.590 --> 00:03:22.780
The demonic villain Master Pandemonium
stole and absorbed the twins, giving him the

00:03:22.780 --> 00:03:26.220
unintentionally hilarious visual of a man
with babies for arms.

00:03:26.500 --> 00:03:30.700
It later turned out that the babies were pieces
of the demonic Mephisto's soul that had been

00:03:30.700 --> 00:03:31.480
blasted off.

00:03:31.700 --> 00:03:36.400
When Wanda wanted children, she unintentionally
siphoned off parts of Mephisto's broken souls

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:37.400
to create them.

00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:41.730
Agatha Harkness was able to banish Mephisto
by erasing Wanda's memory of

00:03:41.730 --> 00:03:46.371
ever having children, which, thanks to her
subconscious reality warping abilities, meant

00:03:46.380 --> 00:03:47.660
that they stopped existing.

00:03:47.680 --> 00:03:48.980
Problem solved, right?

00:03:49.800 --> 00:03:51.100
Avengers: Disassembled

00:03:51.390 --> 00:03:56.120
In the Avengers: Disassembled story arc, Scarlet
Witch hits her breaking point after the Wasp

00:03:56.120 --> 00:03:58.960
accidently reminds her of her memory-wiped
children.

00:03:59.140 --> 00:04:03.200
The psychotic break that follows features
her going on an incredibly violent rampage

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:04.460
against the Avengers.

00:04:04.560 --> 00:04:08.750
Hawkeye doesn't survive, Vision is ripped
in half, Agatha Harkness is discovered as

00:04:08.750 --> 00:04:13.470
a rotting corpse, and Scarlet Witch herself
gets put into the custody of Magneto until

00:04:13.470 --> 00:04:14.830
she can get the help she needs.

00:04:14.830 --> 00:04:16.420
Which is a whole lot of help.

00:04:17.200 --> 00:04:18.140
House of M

00:04:18.680 --> 00:04:23.599
Wanda's reality-warping powers and mental
break lead to the 2005 Marvel crossover event

00:04:23.599 --> 00:04:28.560
House of M, in which Wanda was coerced into
rewriting reality so that mutants are the

00:04:28.560 --> 00:04:30.220
dominant life form on the planet.

00:04:30.440 --> 00:04:34.500
When confronted by the various heroes who
remembered the old world, Wanda responds to

00:04:34.509 --> 00:04:38.419
the stress and guilt by erasing the mutant
genome, turning almost every mutant in the

00:04:38.420 --> 00:04:39.920
world into a powerless human.

00:04:40.300 --> 00:04:41.640
Talk about lashing out.

00:04:42.320 --> 00:04:43.300
Brotherly love

00:04:43.880 --> 00:04:47.900
In the alternate reality of The Ultimates
comic series, Scarlet Witch and Quicksilver's

00:04:47.909 --> 00:04:52.430
co-dependent relationship was rewritten to
be almost explicitly romantic between the

00:04:52.430 --> 00:04:52.930
twins.

00:04:52.940 --> 00:04:57.720
Worse, in Ultimates 3, the Wasp even chides
Captain America for expressing his judgement

00:04:57.720 --> 00:05:02.229
of their romance by telling him that his World
War II sense of morality is outdated in this

00:05:02.229 --> 00:05:02.900
modern world.

00:05:03.300 --> 00:05:03.800
Gross.

00:05:04.380 --> 00:05:06.620
To Avengers: Infinity War and beyond

00:05:06.900 --> 00:05:10.699
With all the storylines mentioned above, you
might be thinking that the Marvel Cinematic

00:05:10.700 --> 00:05:14.980
Universe made the right decision to simplify
both her origin and her superpowers.

00:05:15.129 --> 00:05:19.620
A Scarlet Witch not bound by constant family
revelations and a codependent brother has

00:05:19.620 --> 00:05:20.789
a lot of story potential.

00:05:20.789 --> 00:05:24.600
Still, we'll have to see how that changes
as Disney starts to incorporate Twentieth

00:05:24.600 --> 00:05:27.320
Century Fox concepts with the planned merger.

00:05:27.469 --> 00:05:31.180
Whether that means leaning into the magical
angle like Dr. Strange or reincorporating

00:05:31.180 --> 00:05:34.000
her into the mutant world, just about anything
can happen.

00:05:34.360 --> 00:05:35.780
"I can't control their fear.

00:05:36.360 --> 00:05:37.400
Only my own."

00:05:40.400 --> 00:05:41.460
Well, almost.

00:05:41.740 --> 00:05:46.320
It is probably fair to assume that we won't
be seeing Bova the bovine midwife or Master

00:05:46.320 --> 00:05:49.800
Pandemonium and his baby arms on the big screen
anytime soon.

00:05:49.800 --> 00:05:50.720
Thanks for watching!

